   "Lesson-specific rules: Compare hundreds before tens before ones. A collection with 1 hundred and12 tens and4 ones has value224, equal to a standard 2 hundreds2 tens4 ones. Normalize noncanonical base-ten representations before comparison. 261<313,239>165,224=224. Original source activity essential evidence: Activity1 original actual Mai/Tyler base-ten diagrams; teacher launch Tyler2 hundreds and Mai1 hundred. Original compare 261 (2h6t1o) <313 (3h1t3o),239 (2h3t9o) >165 (1h6t5o), and224 (2h2t4o) EQUAL224 (1h12t4o). Activity2 pupils reason about place values with expanded form and actual pictured blocks; educator must inspect images and physical grouping. Official standards: CCSS:2.NBT.A.4, CCSS:2.NBT.B.8.",
   "ORIGINAL SOURCE (teacher/public math tasks, paraphrased): Original76,76,99,99; 261<313,239>165,224=224 from2h2t4o versus1h12t4o. The source-specific image, physical work and student response require actual educator inspection. Other generated examples in Edulytics are FIRST-PARTY, not copied publisher restricted assessment.",
   "1. Review true original publisher warm-up: Original Number Talk add tens:36+40=76,46+30=76,59+40=99,69+30=99. 2. Examine source student-facing tasks and materials: Activity1 original actual Mai/Tyler base-ten diagrams; teacher launch Tyler2 hundreds and Mai1 hundred. Original compare 261 (2h6t1o) <313 (3h1t3o),239 (2h3t9o) >165 (1h6t5o), and224 (2h2t4o) EQUAL224 (1h12t4o). Activity2 pupils reason about place values with expanded form and actual pictured blocks; educator must inspect images and physical grouping. 3. Show original numeric and place-value strategies: Compare hundreds before tens before ones. A collection with 1 hundred and12 tens and4 ones has value224, equal to a standard 2 hundreds2 tens4 ones. Normalize noncanonical base-ten representations before comparison. 261<313,239>165,224=224. 4. Discuss plausible misconception and accurate solution with specific source values: Comparing number of pieces without recognizing 10 tens=1 hundred. Claiming 1h12t4o is124 is incorrect; it is224. Don't invent image-only other quantities. 5. Finish actual source images/cards/games/drawings with educator; do NOT invent values not available as text. 6. Complete separate original Edulytics numeric practice with exact re-verification and teacher-graded open parts. 7. Preserve teacher assessment boundary: Teacher validates original Mai/Tyler and all published block diagram figures, place value comparison and student verbal defense; original cool-down inaccessible.",
   "Mathematically inappropriate actions: Comparing number of pieces without recognizing 10 tens=1 hundred. Claiming 1h12t4o is124 is incorrect; it is224. Don't invent image-only other quantities. Do not claim numeric answer certifies original image, physical block/card game, number-line dot or class oral practice.",
