  ["IM2021 original Grade2 Unit5 Lesson11 Place Value Comparisons (Part 2). Original True/False:86>80+4 TRUE;400+40+6<846 TRUE;330<300+3 FALSE;500+50>505 TRUE. Activity1 publisher compare521<523,889>878. Arrange four UNIQUE actual numbers810,529,752,495 into source inequalities:529>519,687<752,495<501,810>793; especially810 must fill fourth. Activity2 real Greatest of Them All Stage2 digit card game (remove '10' cards), place each drawn digit in H/T/O irreversibly, larger three-digit number wins round; teacher checks actual cards and strategy. Original source answer 920 greatest and209 smallest from digits2,0,9. Source math: Digits represent hundreds, tens and ones; a comparison can have unique assignment when each source number used ONCE. 810 is the only given value >793, so reserve it there. Forming a THREE-digit number can't start0; digits2,0,9 yield greatest920 and smallest209. True/False uses evaluated expressions, not comparing appearance of symbols. Real teacher tasks: Actual digit cards, source number-line diagrams, multi-solution pupil strategy, partner game outcomes educator only; protected Cool-down omitted.",
